[38;2;124;124;124mA locally closed subset $Y$ of $X$ means $Y = U \cap F$ where $U$ is open and [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$F$ is closed in $X$. Equivalently, $Y$ is open in its closure $\overline{Y}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWe want to show: if $Y \neq \emptyset$ then $Y$ contains a closed point of $X$.[0m

